{"name":"Weather Board","hex":"#9f947d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"weather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The short-term state of the atmosphere at a specific time and place, including the temperature, relative humidity, cloud cover, precipitation, wind, etc.","Unpleasant or destructive atmospheric conditions, and their effects."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Facing towards the flow of a fluid, usually air."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weather"},{"term":"board","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A relatively long, wide and thin piece of any material, usually wood or similar, often for use in construction or furniture-making.","A device (e.g., switchboard) containing electrical switches and other controls and designed to control lights, sound, telephone connections, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To step or climb onto or otherwise enter a ship, aircraft, train or other conveyance.","To provide someone with meals and lodging, usually in exchange for money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/board"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clapboard","blocks":[{"text":"Clapboard, also called clabbard, bevel siding, lap siding, and weatherboard, with regional variation in the definition of those terms, is wooden siding of a building in the form of horizontal boards, often overlapping."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Close-up_of_original_quarter_sawn_riven_oak_clapboards_in_leanto_attic.JPG/330px-Close-up_of_original_quarter_sawn_riven_oak_clapboards_in_leanto_attic.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clapboard","wikidata":"Q382362"},{"title":"Weather","blocks":[{"text":"Weather is the state of the Earth's atmosphere at a specific place and time, typically described in terms of temperature, humidity, cloud cover, and stability. On Earth, most weather phenomena occur in the lowest layer of the planet's atmosphere, the troposphere, just below the stratosphere. Weather refers to day-to-day temperature, precipitation, and other atmospheric conditions, whereas climate is the term for the averaging of atmospheric conditions over longer periods of time. When used without qualification, \"weather\" is generally understood to mean the weather of Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/330px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weather","wikidata":"Q11663"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Stained_wooden_clapboard_siding.jpg/500px-Stained_wooden_clapboard_siding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Stained_wooden_clapboard_siding.jpg/1280px-Stained_wooden_clapboard_siding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Stained_wooden_clapboard_siding.jpg/500px-Stained_wooden_clapboard_siding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clapboard siding stained dark brown","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStained_wooden_clapboard_siding.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Saltbox_Concord_2_cropped.jpg/500px-Saltbox_Concord_2_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Saltbox_Concord_2_cropped.jpg/500px-Saltbox_Concord_2_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Captain William Smith House at Minute Man National Historical 